<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48169" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Thersītes</span></b> , ae,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Θερσίτης,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Greek before
			Troy</i>, <i>famous for his ugliness and
			scurrility</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 13, 233</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. P. 3,
				9, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 11, 31</span></i>.—Hence, <i>a contemptible person</i>, <i><span class="en">Juv. 8,
			269</span></i>; and for <i>a calumniator</i>, <i>reviler</i>, <i><span class="en">Sen.
				Ira, 3, 23, 3</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
